course: dictionary
lesson: 5971
title: Maundy: a word from church life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maundy is a noun, a name for a day or ceremony in church life. Maundy Thursday is the Thursday before Easter, when Christians remember the Last Supper of Jesus with his disciples.
explain: Context helps here. «Passover remembers the Exodus; the Gospels set the Last Supper at Passover time, and Christians remember it on Maundy Thursday, the day before Good Friday.» The sentence tells you Maundy Thursday comes just before Good Friday, so it is part of Holy Week, the week before Easter.
explain: Maundy has more than one meaning. The Maundy is a ceremony where people wash feet, to remember how Jesus served others. In Britain, Maundy money means special silver coins that the king or queen gives to older people.
fact: Maundy Thursday is the Thursday before Easter, in Holy Week.
fact: Maundy Thursday is the day before Good Friday.
fact: The word Maundy comes from Latin «mandatum», meaning «commandment».
fact: Jesus said, «Love one another», and the Maundy reminds people of this.
fact: Maundy money is special silver coins given to older people by the British king or queen.
exercise: «Passover remembers the Exodus; the Gospels set the Last Supper at Passover time, and Christians remember it on Maundy Thursday, the day before Good Friday.» Which day comes straight after Maundy Thursday? | Christmas Day | Midsummer Day | Halloween | *Good Friday
exercise: What is Maundy money? | Coins children find on the way to school | Coins given to older people by the British king or queen | Money paid to join a church choir | *Special silver coins given to older people by the British king or queen
exercise: Where does the word Maundy come from? | *Latin «mandatum», meaning commandment | Greek word for water | Old English word for feet | French word for dinner
test: What does the Maundy ceremony remember? | Jesus riding a donkey into a city | *Jesus washing his disciples' feet to show how to serve others | Jesus feeding five thousand people | Jesus being born in a stable
test: Maundy Thursday is part of which week? | Harvest week | *Holy Week | Half-term week | Bank holiday week
exam: Which name means the Thursday before Good Friday in church life? | *Maundy Thursday | Boxing Day | Shrove Tuesday | Harvest Festival
